      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(infra): drop replacement characters when response snippets truncate UTF-8",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nSeveral bounded diagnostic readers decoded a byte prefix with a normal `TextDecoder` flush. When a size cap split a multi-byte character, that flush invented a trailing replacement character (`�`) in provider errors, `web_fetch` output, embedding errors, memory-host snippets, Voice/SMS errors, and related diagnostics.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis revision moves the invariant to one owner:\n\n- `@openclaw/normalization-core` now provides a one-shot `decodeTextPrefix` helper. Truncated prefixes decode in streaming mode with a fresh decoder, so only an incomplete trailing sequence is discarded; complete bodies still flush and preserve genuinely malformed input.\n- Core infrastructure exposes `readResponseTextPrefix`, which owns bounded byte reads, overflow cancellation, timeout behavior, and prefix decoding.\n- The Plugin SDK exports that narrow reader so Voice and SMS plugins no longer maintain duplicate stream loops.\n- Provider, web, memory-host, embedding, Voice, SMS, and ChatGPT Responses siblings now share the same truncation rule.\n- Successful Voice/SMS JSON bodies remain strict: they still use `readResponseWithLimit` and fail on overflow. Only diagnostic/error prefixes truncate.\n\nThis deletes repeated reader state machines and keeps one canonical prefix-decoding path; it does not add a compatibility shim or config surface.\n\n## User Impact\n\nBounded error and diagnostic text no longer ends with a spurious replacement character merely because OpenClaw stopped at its byte budget. Full response decoding, malformed full-body behavior, character caps, timeout errors, and strict success-body limits remain unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kx47ve0qwsaaevb4g1k2r8bv`: 154 focused tests passed across the normalization, core/provider, web, embedding, Voice, SMS, memory-host, and ChatGPT Responses surfaces.\n- `@openclaw/normalization-core` build passed.\n- Broad touched-path `pnpm check:changed` passed four tsgo lanes plus core/extension lint and guards.\n- Full `pnpm build` passed.\n- Plugin SDK API generation/check passed and the generated baseline hash was refreshed.\n- Touched-file formatting and `git diff --check` passed.\n- Fresh autoreview found no accepted/actionable findings (confidence 0.95).\n\nRegression coverage distinguishes truncated UTF-8 prefixes from malformed complete bodies, checks exact-limit cancellation, fallback charset decoding, UTF-16-safe character caps, strict success-body overflow, and every migrated caller family.\n",
        "branch": "codex/fix-utf8-response-snippet",
